request.description:
The plain form behind Delete and Delete all on `/account/highlights`, so the page works without JavaScript.
Every outcome but a foreign origin is a 303 back to a page (`Cache-Control: private, no-store`):

- signed out (or no database): `/login?next=%2Faccount%2Fhighlights`;
- a body that isn't a form: `/account/highlights?error=invalid`;
- `intent=delete` with an `id` the account has: `/account/highlights?book=<slug>&status=deleted`, the book the
  highlight was in;
- `intent=delete` with a UUID the account doesn't have: `/account/highlights?error=missing`;
- `intent=delete-book` with a `book` slug: `/account/highlights?status=deleted-book` when it deleted at least
  one, else `/account/highlights?error=missing`;
- any other intent, or an `id` that isn't a UUID or a `book` that isn't a slug:
  `/account/highlights?error=invalid`;
- a database failure: `/account/highlights?error=unavailable`.

Notes go with their highlights. The page itself (GET) isn't described here.

